#proof[
  We first make explicit the finite order choices. Choose a spatial target order $k gt.eq 2 s$, enlarged if necessary to improve every bootstrap and continuation norm. The time recovery below uses at most two spatial derivatives for each time derivative. Choose an integer $M$ much larger than $k + 2$ so that, with $theta.alt = \( k + 2 \) \/ M$,
