  $ q^(- 1) partial_v b = cal(A) gamma^(- 1) \( xi_1 - xi_0 \) . $
  The template change at the fixed bootstrap orders is at most $e^(- \( alpha - eta_0 \) T)$ with $eta_0 < alpha \/ 2$. Together with (5.2), this is strictly smaller than $1 / 2 e^(- alpha T \/ 2)$ for large $T$. It improves (5.8), preserves the nondegeneracy margins, and provides the finite Sobolev buffers required for restart.
  We finish the existence argument, since an a priori comparison on a putative full domain would not suffice. On each fixed finite experiment, $q gt.eq q_0 e^(- 2 kappa L_T) > 0$. All requisite finite norms and inverse metrics are bounded up to a possible terminal slice. Use the finite-domain restart in #cite(label("KerrCTwo")) , proof as follows. On an earlier slice take its induced metric and second fundamental form, initialize wave gauge, and extend the smooth slice jets across the interval endpoints on an enlarged margin. Their required finite Sobolev norms and positivity have controlled extensions. Constraints are needed only on the original margin. The reduced wave equation has a positive local existence time depending on those finite norms and the finite positive lapse. Solve the eikonal pair and angular transport from the slice with their inherited values. Transversality and invertibility persist on a smaller margin for a time bounded below at this fixed $T$.
