#thm([Lemma 7.2.])[
  (Loop jets and the quadratic coefficient).  #emph[Uniformly in the observation positions and $X in cal(X)$, 
#[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(7.10)")
 $ sup_(0 lt.eq l lt.eq 17 l_T) parallel partial_l^18 H_(x \, X) \( l \) parallel lt.eq Q_T . $ <ho:jet-bound>]

 The quadratic Taylor coefficient $C_2 \( x \, X \)$ of $H_(x \, X) \( l \) - upright("Id")$ is the matrix, in $F \( x \)$, of $plus.minus R \( partial_v \, r X \)$. Consequently 
#[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(7.11)")
 $ g #scale(x: 120%, y: 120%)[\(] C_2 \( x \, X \) F_1 \, X #scale(x: 120%, y: 120%)[\)] = plus.minus R \( partial_v \, X \, partial_v \, X \) = plus.minus D \( X \, X \) . $ <ho:curvature-cancellation>]

 The same curvature and loop-orientation convention fixes the signs.]
